% Wave-4 batch A capstone: the real upstream SATySFi 0.1 `std-ja-report`
% document class (dist-v01/packages/std-ja-report.satyh — the report
% sibling of std-ja-book, adding chapters/theorem environments and
% `page-break-multicolumn`/`hook-page-break-block` instead of a
% title-page+TOC), driving the FULL pipeline: V0_1 lex -> cst_v1 parse ->
% loader (`@require:` transitive resolution across annot/math/code/
% footnote-scheme/hyph-english/unidata/the 4 font stand-ins/the stdlib
% leaf packages/ref) -> v1 lowering -> shared elaborate/typecheck(V0_1)/
% sealing -> eval -> line break -> page break (this is the FIRST fixture
% to exercise `page-break-multicolumn`'s V0_1 arm end to end — previously
% only type-table-registered, see `primitives.rs`'s
% `prim_page_break_multicolumn_v01` doc comment) -> PDF. Latin-only,
% math-free, \figure never called (its baked-in `図` literal needs CJK
% glyph coverage the single-DejaVu-face G7 font stand-in cannot provide),
% mirroring `v01-stdja.saty`'s/`v01-stdja-book.saty`'s Latin-only-body
% discipline.
@require: std-ja-report

StdJaReport.document (|
  title  = {SATySFi in Rust: The Report Capstone},
  author = {The Vendoring Agents},
|) '<
  +StdJaReport.chapter{Introduction}<
    +StdJaReport.p {
      This is a real upstream SATySFi 0.1 document class, std-ja-report,
      rendered end to end through the Rust port.
    }
    +StdJaReport.section{Background}<
      +StdJaReport.p {
        The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.
      }
      +StdJaReport.definition ?(word = {Widget}){
        A widget is a thing that this document defines for the purpose of
        \StdJaReport.emph{testing} theorem environments.
      }
      +StdJaReport.theorem{
        Every widget \StdJaReport.dfn{fits} inside its own paragraph.
      }
      +StdJaReport.proof{
        This follows directly from the definition above.
      }
    >
  >
  +StdJaReport.chapter{Conclusion}<
    +StdJaReport.p {
      This concludes the report capstone document.\StdJaReport.footnote{A trailing footnote, proving FootnoteScheme.main renders through the multicolumn page-break path.}
    }
  >
>
